    "effectivePlan" : "Aim for two spade tricks, two hearts, two clubs and three diamonds. Lead D3 and duck in dummy, normally playing D5, to concede a diamond before spending either honor. Recover control with the spade queen or a South-side heart or club winner, preserving dummy's club ace. Then lead South's remaining diamond toward KQ. On a 3–3 break, if that honor loses to the ace, enter dummy with CA and cash its remaining honor and two long diamonds. If the honor wins, continue the other honor to force out the ace, then use CA to cash the two established diamonds. Thus both diamond concessions occur before spending the final entry. Against a club switch, arrange to win with South's king rather than dummy's ace where possible. Avoid premature side-suit cashing. Reassess adverse diamond breaks from the actual cards; three diamond tricks are not guaranteed against every distribution. Long defensive spades remain a danger, so develop diamonds without delay.",
